# loom and C11 (verus/WEAKMEM.md): non-test bitmap.rs writes a bitmap word
# only through these wrappers, and class/table.rs calls no atomic write
# method but the owner word's store (tests/loom/tests/access.rs), so a
# bitmap word's permission value reads as the last write in its
# modification order. `FORK_SIGMASK` is a word these wrappers also read
# (`api::saved_sigmask`'s `load`): its one write is `api::save_sigmask`'s
# raw `store`, through no permission (access.rs), and that the permission
# `api::resume::resumed` mints holds the stored mask is
# `api::resume::axiom_fork_resumed`'s premise; no model covers it. C++20's coherence
# rules ([intro.races]) give a load a write no older than the last one
# that happens before it; `fetch_or` and `fetch_and` are
# read-modify-writes, which read the last value for every ordering
# ([atomics.order] p10). The claim's `Acquire` `fetch_or` and the release's
# `Release` `fetch_and` order one slot owner's writes before the next
# owner's (a release/acquire pair, [atomics.order] p2); the bitmap models
# check that, and the free models the free path's `Relaxed` bit test, on
# copies of the bitmap and table steps (tests/loom/tests/pins.rs). The
# GenMC bitmap cases run `store`, `fetch_or` and `fetch_and` as they are
# over `core`'s atomic, inside pinned copies of the bitmap steps
# (tests/genmc/bitmap.rs, `GENMC_PINS`), with the permissions erased
# (verus/WEAKMEM.md, "GenMC"); only `bitmap_init_published` runs `store`
# while another thread reads, no case runs the free path's `load`, and
# none sees `WordPerm`'s value.
# `WordPerm` is the abstraction itself: its content is these contracts
# and that a word's writes go through them.
WordPerm	atomics primitive	loom/GenMC	trusted (partly checked, loom: bitmap::loom_bitmap_release_then_reserve, bitmap::loom_bitmap_two_claimers and bitmap::loom_bitmap_init_is_published; not checked: that the type's value is its word's last write, the C11 argument above (the models check the wrappers' orderings, running the wrappers as they are, in the configurations tests/loom/src/bitmap.rs states, and no model sees the ghost value), which tests/loom/tests/access.rs backs by matching source text, for the bitmap words, and for `FORK_SIGMASK` only that `api::save_sigmask`'s raw `store` is its one write (its permission's value is `api::resume::axiom_fork_resumed`'s premise, and no model covers it))	contract 3518268196, body 1324333092
# Kani runs each wrapper on a real atomic, one thread (src/kani/atomic.rs).
